1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
In the 2026.0 version, it is optimized that when you open the ZFAB file, you can choose the functions of different materials and attributes, and you can change the material in the correct way.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:27,000
In the previous version, press the Ctrl key to drag the fabric to the object window, and you can choose to load different materials and attributes.

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In the 2026.0 version, we optimized this function experience.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
First, select the fabric in the object window.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
In the property editor, click the button to open the fabric.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
In the tab, select Open, select Material.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
In the folder, select the fabric file and click Open.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
In the window where the fabric is opened, you can give the front, back, and side of the fabric.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Choose whether to open the selected material or physical attribute.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
You can choose to only increase the front fabric and cancel the selection of the reverse fabric.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Click OK.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
You can see the effect of the 3D window.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The front and side fabrics have been updated.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The reverse fabric maintains the original fabric settings.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Open the simulation to check the physical properties of the material.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
In the property editor, the fabric is in the right side of the right side of the side-switch label.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
A new exchange is added to the back material button.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Press the left button.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
In the 3D window, you can see that the front and back fabric of the fabric match each other.

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Switch to the reverse if the hook is used with the same material on the front.

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
At this time, the button to switch between the front and the back material will disappear.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The cancel hook option will appear again.

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Through this update, when opening the GFAB file,

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:52,000
users can quickly open the required part and one-click to switch to the front and back material.

25
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
In the 2026.0 version,

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
we optimized the user interface and size adjustment behavior of the GFAB editor,

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
which provides a more concise user page and a more convenient workflow.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Let's take a look at the interface after the update and the editing process after the update.

29
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
In the previous version,

30
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
when processing a custom GFAB,

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:21,000
the properties such as the rough line thickness, the number of rows per inch, the number of rows per inch and the thickness of the fabric will be displayed directly in the property editor and can be directly edited.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
In the latest update,

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
these specific options have been removed from the property editor.

34
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
If we want to modify these values,

35
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
we need to enter the GFAB editor.

36
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
After removing these parameters,

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
the property editor's current property list is more concise,

38
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:44,000
and the detailed needle parameters are managed specifically in a specific GFAB editor.

39
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
If you want to adjust the size of the GFAB,

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
you can use the GFAB loop on the upper right corner of the GFAB editor.

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
You can also adjust the GFAB loop function.

42
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
After adjusting the number of rows and horizontal lines,

43
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
you can click the button to adjust the size of the GFAB loop.

44
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
More importantly,

45
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
in this process,

46
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
your existing needle design will be completely preserved.

47
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
In addition,

48
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
if you need to completely reset the design content,

49
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
the window in the lower left corner has been added a reset status button.

50
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Clicking this button will immediately reset all the needles in the window as default needles,

51
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
and you can start designing again.

52
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
The update of the GFAB editor in the 2026.0 version

53
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
provides you with a more concentrated and efficient environment in the needle design process.

54
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
In addition,

55
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
the GFAB editor also received another update.

56
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
In the 2026.0 version,

57
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
we expanded the reset and recovery functions to the GFAB editor,

58
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,000
and thus realized a more flexible and efficient editing process.

59
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
You can use the main menu,

60
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
navigation to edit,

61
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
cancel,

62
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
and restore to use these commands.

63
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
For a more efficient work process,

64
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:04,000
